Z||000000||84Bill||05-04-2001||11:27 PM||||Ok for those of us honored enough and some who are not and even maybe you v6 guys. I am going to soup up a 2.5 engine and I thaught it would be cool to include you guys on some of the decisions I need to make and some general advice. I will post reports and info streaming avi's and pictures of the projects progress on my web site. Since the site is not quite ready yet I will post my first question here. <P>I have 3 2.5 engines at my disposal in different conditions <BR>WHITCH one should I use<P>1) an 88 DIS engine 111,000 miles. I hear that you can reprogram the proms timing curve and other cool things.<P>2) an 86 with 130,000 (in florida will have in 3 weeks) standard ignition was a good strong engine and has my beloved 5 speed tranny attached with new fly, clutch, throw bearing and PP. <P>3) an 84 replacement engine with 178,000 already on the stand. this one had the bad vibration and uppon dropping the oil pan I found a piston that moves in the bore waaaaay to easily.<P>Leme know what you think<P>Pics of the 88 and 84 will be on my site in about an hour. the site may be down till then..<P>Oh duh <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Uaana||05-05-2001||12:29 AM||||Just my 2c but I'd go with the 86 and standard ignition. Custom proms are really neat and all but I prefer reliable. Plus depending on the mods you make, lots easier to fiddle and adjust for max performance without having to drop $$$$ in custom programing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrgone||05-05-2001||12:54 AM||||cool! id like to see that, as alot of us poor 2.5 dukes (like myself, 86 2m4 5sp).... get picked on because we are cylindrically challenged.<P>a few more ponies would wipe my tears.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||05-05-2001||01:52 AM||||Go with #2.  It's the obvious choice.  Same reason as mentioned above.  Good luck.  Can't wait to hear more.<BR>||||reg||6
