Z||000005||Mach10||05-05-2001||12:36 PM||||get a 6-cylinder!<P>-Sorry, someone ALWAYS has to say something like that on these kinds of threads  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you aren't going to use a force-air induction system or NOS system, consider taking the CR of the pistons through the roof. The Duck won't be able to spin up to the revs that you can get with DOHC engines, so make the engine turn HARDER, not faster (A concept that Ricey-boyz haven't grasped yet...). It's going to be a chore to get the fuel curves right, but I figure that you can get 300Hp from that motor if you do it right. Just think along the lines of the SD-Duck.||||reg||6
Z||000006||84Bill||05-05-2001||05:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>get a 6-cylinder!<P>-Sorry, someone ALWAYS has to say something like that on these kinds of threads   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you aren't going to use a force-air induction system or NOS system, </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I knew it wouldnt be long b4 someone said get a six! but my duke, if done right will have the same or more HP than a stock six.<P>Nah the non superduty dukes cant take the strain of those kinds ultra high HP mods. Now if I had a superduty now that would do the trick. I've heard of 350 HP! from them with NOS and they will do that all day long.<P>||||reg||1
